      <h2 id="identity-provider-htpasswd-CR_configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Sample htpasswd CR<a href="#identity-provider-htpasswd-CR_configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>The following custom resource (CR) shows the parameters and acceptable values for an htpasswd identity provider.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: config.openshift.io/v1\nkind: OAuth\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster\nspec:\n  identityProviders:\n  - name: my_htpasswd_provider (1)\n    mappingMethod: claim (2)\n    type: HTPasswd\n    htpasswd:\n      fileData:\n        name: htpass-secret (3)"} lang="yaml" title="htpasswd CR" />
      <ol>
      <li>This provider name is prefixed to provider user names to form an identity name.</li>
      <li>Controls how mappings are established between this provider’s identities and <code>User</code> objects.</li>
      <li>An existing secret containing a file generated using <a href="http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/programs/htpasswd.html"><code>htpasswd</code></a>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Additional resources</strong></p>
      <ul><li>See <a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/authentication/understanding-identity-provider#identity-provider-parameters_understanding-identity-provider">Identity provider parameters</a> for information on parameters, such as <code>mappingMethod</code>, that are common to all identity providers.</li></ul>
      <h2 id="add-identity-provider_configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Adding an identity provider to your cluster<a href="#add-identity-provider_configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Apply the identity provider custom resource (CR) to your cluster so users can authenticate with the configured identity provider.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You installed an OpenShift Container Platform cluster.</li>
      <li>You defined the CR for your identity provider.</li>
      <li>You are logged in as an administrator.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Apply the defined CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f </path/to/CR>"} lang="terminal" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>If a CR does not exist, <code>oc apply</code> creates a new CR and might trigger the following warning: <code>Warning: oc apply should be used on resources created by either oc create --save-config or oc apply</code>. In this case you can safely ignore this warning.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      <li>
      Log in to the cluster as a user from your identity provider, entering the password when prompted. Run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc login -u <username>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Confirm that the user logged in successfully and that the username displays by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc whoami"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="identity-provider-htpasswd-update-users_configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Updating users for an htpasswd identity provider<a href="#identity-provider-htpasswd-update-users_configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>You can add or remove users from an existing htpasswd identity provider.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have created a <code>Secret</code> object that contains the htpasswd user file. This procedure assumes that it is named <code>htpass-secret</code>.</li>
      <li>You have configured an htpasswd identity provider. This procedure assumes that it is named <code>my_htpasswd_provider</code>.</li>
      <li>You have access to the <code>htpasswd</code> utility. On Red Hat Enterprise Linux this is available by installing the <code>httpd-tools</code> package.</li>
      <li>You have cluster administrator privileges.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Retrieve the htpasswd file from the <code>htpass-secret</code> <code>Secret</code> object and save the file to your file system:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get secret htpass-secret -ojsonpath={.data.htpasswd} -n openshift-config | base64 --decode > users.htpasswd"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Add or remove users from the <code>users.htpasswd</code> file.
      <ul>
      <li>
      To add a new user:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ htpasswd -bB users.htpasswd <username> <password>"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"Adding password for user <username>"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To remove an existing user:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ htpasswd -D users.htpasswd <username>"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"Deleting password for user <username>"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
      Replace the <code>htpass-secret</code> <code>Secret</code> object with the updated users in the <code>users.htpasswd</code> file:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create secret generic htpass-secret --from-file=htpasswd=users.htpasswd --dry-run=client -o yaml -n openshift-config | oc replace -f -"} lang="terminal" />
      <Alert variant="tip" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Tip</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You can alternatively apply the following YAML to replace the secret:</p>
          <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: Secret\nmetadata:\n  name: htpass-secret\n  namespace: openshift-config\ntype: Opaque\ndata:\n  htpasswd: <base64_encoded_htpasswd_file_contents>"} lang="yaml" />
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      <li>
      If you removed one or more users, you must additionally remove existing resources for each user.
      <ol>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>User</code> object:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete user <username>"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"user.user.openshift.io \"<username>\" deleted"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      <p>Be sure to remove the user, otherwise the user can continue using their token as long as it has not expired.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>Identity</code> object for the user:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete identity my_htpasswd_provider:<username>"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"identity.user.openshift.io \"my_htpasswd_provider:<username>\" deleted"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="identity-provider-configuring-using-the-web-console_configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring identity providers using the web console<a href="#identity-provider-configuring-using-the-web-console_configuring-htpasswd-identity-provider" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Configure your identity provider (IDP) through the web console instead of the CLI.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You must be logged in to the web console as a cluster administrator.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>Navigate to <strong>Administration</strong> -&gt; <strong>Cluster Settings</strong>.</li>
      <li>Under the <strong>Configuration</strong> tab, click <strong>OAuth</strong>.</li>
      <li>Under the <strong>Identity Providers</strong> section, select your identity provider from the <strong>Add</strong> drop-down menu.</li>
      </ol>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You can specify multiple IDPs through the web console without overwriting existing IDPs.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
    </article>
